From 236966116292c674e7dfa99d59dbad6cec8874d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Liang Jun Chen <151501304+senti0726@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:30:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 12/18] fix: accept scalar values where a vector is expected
 (#652)

* fix: accept scalar values where a vector is expected

Wallpaper Engine is not consistent about how it serialises vector fields.
The same field can be written either as a "x y" string or as a bare scalar
meaning the same value on every component - text objects in particular write
`"padding": "32.00000 32.00000"` in some scenes and `"padding": 32` in others.

JsonExtensions::get<glm::vec<...>> assumed the string form unconditionally and
called get<std::string>() on the node, so whichever form a scene did not use
threw type_error.302 and aborted before the wallpaper could load.

Accept both forms: broadcast a JSON number across every component, and parse
the string form as before.

TextData::padding was also typed `int`, which could only ever hold the scalar
form. It is a 2-component value, so make it a glm::vec2 and read it through
the same path.

Tested against 105 scene packages: 4 still fail (unrelated shader and missing
texture problems), the rest load. No scene that previously loaded regressed.

Refs #96

